  "articleBody": "Before hiring a contractor for a primary suite addition, define the desired rooms, measure the available building area, collect property records, and ask how design, permits, structural work, utilities, and construction will be coordinated. Compare proposals by scope rather than price alone. A clear plan should identify assumptions, exclusions, finish allowances, approval responsibilities, and the conditions that could change the final cost.",
